course: dictionary
lesson: 7623
title: Probe: a tool or a search
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can be a thing or an action, and the sentence tells you which. «Its surface was mapped by radar, for example by the Magellan probe in the 1990s.» Here probe is a thing: a spacecraft with no people in it, sent to explore.
explain: «A long bill probes the mud for food.» Now probes is an action. The bird pushes its bill into the mud to search. The clues are the mud and for food, so to probe means to explore something by pushing into it.
explain: Probe can also mean to look into something carefully or ask lots of questions. «Reporters probe a mystery.» Try your meaning in the sentence: they look into the mystery carefully, so the meaning fits.
fact: A probe is a spacecraft with no people in it, sent to explore planets and space.
fact: A probe can also be a thin tool used to measure something, such as a temperature probe.
fact: As a verb, «probe» means to look into something carefully or to push a tool or finger into something to explore it.
fact: In 2005 the European «Huygens probe» parachuted onto Titan.
fact: Some words are both nouns and verbs, so the sentence shows which one it is.
exercise: «Its surface was mapped by radar, for example by the Magellan probe in the 1990s.» In this sentence, what is a probe? | *A spacecraft with no people in it | A kind of thick cloud | A question asked by a reporter | A bird's long bill
exercise: «A long bill probes the mud for food.» What does probes mean here? | Builds a nest out of mud | Sings loudly to its friends | *Pushes into the mud to explore it for food | Flies high over the marsh
exercise: Nadia says a reporter will probe a mystery. What does probe mean? | *Look into it carefully and ask questions | Wrap it in paper | Ignore it completely | Forget it quickly
test: «A temperature probe connected to a computer records readings.» What is a temperature probe? | A spacecraft sent to Titan | A cold drink in a glass | *A thin tool used to measure temperature | A bird that wades in marshes
test: «Probe deeper» means what? | Stop looking straight away | Dig a hole in the ground | Read the book backwards | *Look more carefully and find out more
exam: Which sentence uses probe as a verb? | *Ella will probe the sand with a stick to see how deep it is | The temperature probe is on the desk | The Huygens probe landed on Titan | Space probes are sent far away
